  "text": "Here's a function that counts word frequencies ignoring case and punctuation:\n\n```python\nimport string\n\ndef word_histogram(text):\n    text = text.lower()\n    for punc in string.punctuation:\n        text = text.replace(punc, ' ')\n    words = text.split()\n    freq = {}\n    for word in words:\n        freq[word] = freq.get(word, 0) + 1\n    return freq\n```\n\nThis function converts the input text to lowercase to ignore case, replaces punctuation with spaces, splits the text into words, and then counts each word's frequency using a dictionary. The unit tests provided in the query should pass with this implementation.",
